INTRODUCTION
In today’s interconnected world, people communicate in multiple languages across digital platforms. 
Automatically detecting the language of text is essential for applications such as translation services, sentiment analysis, and conversational AI.
The Language Detection NLP system is designed to analyze user input and identify the language with high accuracy.
By leveraging statistical models and probability scores, the system ensures reliable detection even for short text samples.

OBJECTIVES
The main objectives of the project are:
1.	To detect the language of user-provided text using NLP techniques.
2.	To provide both the language code and human-readable language name.
3.	To display probability scores for multiple possible languages.
4.	To handle multilingual inputs with high accuracy.
5.	To create an interactive system where users can test language detection in real time.

METHODOLOGY
1. Input Handling
Users enter text in any language. The system accepts sentences or phrases and processes them for detection.
2. Language Detection
The langdetect library is used to identify the language.
•	If the text is too short (less than three words), the system defaults to English for stability.
•	Probabilities for multiple candidate languages are calculated.
3. Output
The system displays:
•	Detected language code (e.g., en, fr, te).
•	Language name (e.g., English, French, Telugu).
•	Probability distribution of possible languages.
4. User Interaction
The program runs in a loop, allowing users to test multiple sentences until they type exit to stop.
TECHNOLOGIES USED
•	Python – Programming language
•	langdetect – Language detection library
•	Regular Expressions (Regex) – Input validation
•	Probability Models – For multilingual detection confidence
